# Concierge Agent — environment variables
#
# The agent and skill files do NOT read this file. Their settings are the
# {{PLACEHOLDER}} values listed in the README, which you replace in the files.
#
# This file is for the command-line tools YOU supply (email, PMS, tracker,
# calendar). If those tools read credentials from a `.env`, copy this file to
# `.env` and add them there. If they keep credentials elsewhere (a keychain,
# their own config), you do not need a `.env` at all.
#
# Never commit your real `.env` to git. The included .gitignore excludes it.

# ============================================================
# Example: credentials for a Cloudbeds lookup / notes script
# ============================================================
# Use the variable names your own scripts expect.

# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_ID=""
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# CLOUDBEDS_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
# CLOUDBEDS_REFRESH_TOKEN=""
